<article class="env-lemma" id="0GJ1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GJ1">Lemma <span data-tag="0GJ1">59.70.9</span>.</a> Consider a cartesian diagram of schemes </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ U \ar[d]_ g \ar[r]_{j'} &  X \ar[d]^ f \\  V \ar[r]^ j &  Y }  \]
</div>
  <p> where $f$ is finite and $j$ is an open immersion. Then $f_* \circ j'_! = j_! \circ g_*$ as functors $\textit{Ab}(U_{\acute{e}tale}) \to \textit{Ab}(Y_{\acute{e}tale})$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathcal{F}$ be an object of $\textit{Ab}(U_{\acute{e}tale})$. Let $\overline{y}$ be a geometric point of $Y$ not contained in the open $V$. Then 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  (f_*j'_!\mathcal{F})_{\overline{y}} = \bigoplus \nolimits _{\overline{x},\  f(\overline{x}) = \overline{y}} (j'_!\mathcal{F})_{\overline{x}} = 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by Proposition <a href="/tag/03QP" data-tag="03QP">59.55.2</a> and because the stalk of $j'_!\mathcal{F}$ at $\overline{x} \not\in U$ are zero by Lemma <a href="/tag/0F70" data-tag="0F70">59.70.4</a>. On the other hand, we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  j^{-1}f_*j'_!\mathcal{F} = g_*(j')^{-1}j'_!\mathcal{F} = g_*\mathcal{F}  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by Lemmas <a href="/tag/0959" data-tag="0959">59.55.3</a> and <a href="/tag/0F70" data-tag="0F70">59.70.4</a>. Hence by the characterization of $j_!$ in Lemma <a href="/tag/0F70" data-tag="0F70">59.70.4</a> we see that $f_*j'_!\mathcal{F} = j_!g_*\mathcal{F}$. We omit the verification that this identification is functorial in $\mathcal{F}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>